test for_loop_over_array
mode run
file examples/forloop.dusk
out 6\n
---
# The counted loop (1.16.0): `for i in lo..hi` and `for i in lo..hi by k` count
# through a half open range. The bounds are evaluated once, low first, the binder
# is a fresh immutable int64 per iteration, and the step is a nonzero integer
# literal whose sign picks the comparison, so the direction is known at compile
# time. The run records pin the counts and the evaluation order; the check_fail
# twins pin every form the head refuses.
test forrange_counts_up
mode run
file examples/forrange_up.dusk
out 0\n1\n2\n3\n4\n
