# Doc rendering (1.6.1 W5+W6): `dusk doc` normalizes each attached doc block and
# renders the module as markdown. A dangling block or a drift against the signature
# is a fault with a non-zero exit and nothing on stdout; a clean file prints the
# markdown. Tool mode compares stdout and the exit code.
test doc_attach_basic
mode tool
argv doc examples/doc_attach_basic.dusk
out # Module doc_attach_basic\n\nParadigm: procedural\n\nThe doc_attach_basic module shows every place a doc block binds: the module itself, a top-level function, a struct, an enum, an interface and its method, an impl method, and a monad method. It also mixes the gutter and non-gutter styles and puts an at-word inside an example.\n\n## Functions\n\n### add\n\n```dusk\nfunc add(a: int64, b: int64) -> int64\n```\n\nAdds two numbers, in the gutter style.\n\nParameters:\n\n- `a`: the first addend\n- `b`: the second addend\n\nReturns: the sum of a and b\n\n### Box.unit\n\n```dusk\nexport func Box.unit<A>(x: A) -> Box<A>\n```\n\nunit lifts a value into a Box.\n\nParameters:\n\n- `x`: the value to lift\n\nReturns: a Box holding x\n\n### Box.bind\n\n```dusk\nexport func Box.bind<A, B>(m: Box<A>, f: (A) -> Box<B>) -> Box<B>\n```\n\n### main\n\n```dusk\nfunc main() -> int32\n```\n\n## Structs\n\n### Point\n\n```dusk\nstruct Point {\n    x: int64,\n    y: int64,\n}\n```\n\nA point in the plane, compact non-gutter style.\n\n### Host\n\n```dusk\nstruct Host {\n    id: int64,\n}\n```\n\n## Enums\n\n### Shape\n\n```dusk\nenum Shape {\n    Circle,\n    Square,\n}\n```\n\nThe shapes the renderer knows.\n\nExample:\n\n```dusk\ns := Shape.Circle\n@import std.io is content inside an example, not a tag\n```\n\n## Interfaces\n\n### Greeter\n\n```dusk\ninterface Greeter {\n    greet() -> int64\n}\n```\n\nAnything that can greet.\n\n#### greet\n\n```dusk\ngreet() -> int64\n```\n\ngreet returns a greeting code.\n\n## Impls\n\n### impl Greeter for Host\n\n#### greet\n\n```dusk\nfunc greet() -> int64\n```\n\ngreet on Host returns the host id.\n\nReturns: the stored id\n
code 0
---
