# Doc fixes (1.7.0 W4): a `@param` may name a generic type parameter as well as a
# value parameter, and a doc block before an `impl` head attaches to the impl and
# renders as its header prose. A doc before a foreign block still dangles, and the
# dangling message now names impl among the attachment targets.
test doc_param_generic
mode tool
argv doc examples/doc_param_generic.dusk
out # Module doc_param_generic\n\nParadigm: procedural\n\n## Functions\n\n### id\n\n```dusk\nexport func id<T>(x: T) -> T\n```\n\nReturns its argument unchanged.\n\nParameters:\n\n- `T`: the value type\n- `x`: the value to return\n\nReturns: the same value\n
