# check --json (1.7.1 W7): the LSP machine face for `dusk check`. stdout is exactly
# one JSON document plus a trailing newline in every outcome, clean or faulty; stderr
# stays silent and the exit code mirrors the human check, 0 clean and 1 with any
# diagnostic. Emission order is the human order: loader stream, resolve, typeck, mono,
# ground. Each diagnostic names the file its span lands in, its file-local byte span,
# and 1-based scalar line and column; an unresolvable import carries a null span.
test checkjson_clean
mode tool
argv check --json examples/checkjson_clean.dusk
out {\n  "file": "examples/checkjson_clean.dusk",\n  "ok": true,\n  "diagnostics": []\n}\n
code 0
---
