---
# owning func (1.9.0): a func head may declare `owning`, marking its call
# result the caller's own value. The checker classifies and exempts on the marker
# exactly as it does on the vec_take/map_take table, the two unioned for the 1.9.0
# ratchet bridge. A pointer result blesses as an owner (freed, moved, direct-freed); a
# generic result at a scalar instantiation is inert; a lying marker faults through the
# generation backstop. The head rejects async, export "C", a method, void, and tuple
# returns, and a lone owning demands a func.
test owning_basic
mode run
file examples/owning_basic.dusk
out 10\n20\n1\n
