# A local binding shadows an imported module's name: a call through a name the function
# itself bound is a method call on that value, not a call into the module. The qualified
# call fold reads the binding scopes to tell them apart, so the parameter and the let both
# reach the method, while the same spelling in a function that binds nothing still folds to
# the module's free function. Before the fold saw bindings this printed the module's 7 for
# all three, silently, with a clean check.
test a_local_binding_shadows_an_imported_module_name
mode run
file examples/foldshadow_main.dusk
out 400\n500\n7\n
