---
# The separator between match arms exists to find the end of a one line arm, and a closing
# brace already ends one, so an arm that ends in a brace may drop its comma: its own block,
# or the match, if, or lambda it evaluates. Every existing arm keeps its comma, so this
# only accepts a shape that used to be named as a missing token.
test a_match_arm_that_ends_in_a_brace_may_omit_its_comma
mode run
