---
# An impl block has no visibility of its own: a method is reachable exactly where its
# receiver type is. The keyword parsed and its flag was dropped, so an export on an impl
# read as an export that did nothing.
test an_impl_block_takes_no_export
mode check_fail
file examples/exportimpl_fail.dusk
err_has an impl takes no export; its methods follow the receiver type
---
# A foreign block has no visibility of its own: its functions are the C symbols they name,
# never privatized and never renamed, so every importer reaches them by those names
# whatever is written in front of the block. The keyword parsed and its flag was dropped,
# so an export on a foreign block read as an export that did nothing. std.math carried one
# of these; dropping it changes nothing, which is the point.
test a_foreign_block_takes_no_export
mode check_fail
file examples/exportforeign_fail.dusk
err_has a foreign block takes no export; its functions are reached by their own names
