# The other direction of the same rule. A package is compiled into the program that
# requires it, so the project's own parse is physically there, and the dependency was
# written without it and cannot reach it. The refusal is spelled at the dependency's file,
# by its manifest relative path.
test a_package_cannot_reach_a_name_the_project_declares
mode check_fail
